> not just chapter headings.
>
> Anyway, Ch 4 is about internationalization and message
> catalogs. Just before the message catalog piece, I used
> this quote:
>
>      "Lojban is culturally fully neutral. Its vocabulary was
>      built algorithmically using today's six most widely
>      spoken languages: Chinese, Hindi, English, Russian,
>      Spanish, and Arabic."
>          -- _What is Lojban?_, Nick Nicholas and John Cowan
>
> Just in case anyone cares. I hope it piques some
> readers' interest...
